 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Classify each of the following probabilities as theoretical, empirical, or subjective.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 515968,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You have entered a raffle with 500 entrants. Your probability of winning is 0.2%.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "theoretical"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>This is theoretical. You know that 500 people have tickets.</p>\n<p>For an experiment whose sample space <i>S</i> consists of equally likely outcomes, the theoretical probability of the event <i>E</i> is <span data-math=\"P(E) = \\frac{{n(E)}}{{n(S)}}\"></span>, where <i>n</i>(<i>E</i>) and <i>n</i>(<i>S</i>) denote the number of outcomes in the event and in the sample space, respectively.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"P{\\rm{(winning)}} =  \\frac{1}{{500}} = 0.002 = 0.2\\% \"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 515969,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Your little brother takes the bus to school each morning. On the first day of school, you believe that the probability that the bus arrives between 7:15 AM and 7:30 AM is about 80%.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "subjective"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "When you see “you believe,” you know this is not yet based on facts. It is the first day of school. The person has not yet seen the bus arrive and is guessing when it will arrive. This is subjective, which is based on instinct."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 515970,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Your little brother takes the bus to school each morning. On the last day of school, you believe that the probability that the bus arrives between 7:15 AM and 7:30 AM is about 73%.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "empirical"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "This is the last day of school. The person is basing the probability on previous replications of the experiment, having seen the bus arrive repeatedly between those times. This is empirical."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
